    <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">TurnKey Internet is the right pick for North American developers who want a long-stable, family-owned VPS provider running on renewable energy, and who don't need global datacenter coverage. The 27-year track record is a real signal — most VPS brands we review have been around for 5-10 years. The Latham, NY datacenter gives sub-10ms latency to NYC, Boston, and Toronto, and the 100% renewable energy posture is rare in this segment. The trade-offs are clear: $7.95/mo is roughly 4x RackNerd's $1.99, and there's no EU or APAC option. If you serve a North American audience and value vendor stability + green infrastructure, TurnKey Internet is a strong pick. If you need global reach or the lowest possible price, look at RackNerd (8 datacenters, $1.99/yr) or Vultr (32 locations, $2.50/mo).</p>
